<p dir="auto">Jeff-0.8B decides in 29–49 ms per move on an M4 Max; Jev's published Doom run took 212 ms per call over its API. The
two times were not measured on the same hardware. To play them yourself:</p>
<div dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="uv sync --extra games
uv run python -m jeff.games --game doom --player jeff --criteria situation --url http://127.0.0.1:8765 --video --out runs/games/doom.json
uv run python -m jeff.games --game frogger --player jeff --criteria outcomes --url http://127.0.0.1:8765 --out runs/games/frogger.json
uv run python -m jeff.games --game pacman --player rule --out runs/games/pacman-rule.json"><pre>uv sync --extra games
uv run python -m jeff.games --game doom --player jeff --criteria situation --url http://127.0.0.1:8765 --video --out runs/games/doom.json
uv run python -m jeff.games --game frogger --player jeff --criteria outcomes --url http://127.0.0.1:8765 --out runs/games/frogger.json
uv run python -m jeff.games --game pacman --player rule --out runs/games/pacman-rule.json</pre></div>
<p dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" dir="auto">Speed and size</h2><a id="user-content-speed-and-size" aria-label="Permalink: Speed and size" href="#speed-and-size"></a></p>
<p dir="auto">Median time per decision over the same 200 benchmark questions (about 200 input tokens each), one question at a time,
from raw text to probabilities:</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Model</th>
<th>Parameters</th>
<th>Weights (16-bit)</th>
<th>NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000</th>
<th>Apple M4 Max (MLX)</th>
<th>CPU (32 threads)</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
